    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Maintenance</span>
    <h1>Motorbike Fuel in Hanoi</h1>
    <p>Fuel is the simplest part of riding in Vietnam, and knowing how it works removes the last excuse for not renting a bike. Petrol stations are dense in Hanoi, fueling is fast, and the system has its own small etiquette that takes one visit to learn. This guide covers how stations work here, what fuel types you will see at the pumps, how to refuel a rental bike, and how to plan fuel for everything from city errands to full day trips.</p>
    <p>It belongs to the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a> hub, which collects the everyday skills behind riding in Hanoi. For trip planning, see the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/">Hanoi motorbike trips</a> hub, and for the rental process itself, start with <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/how-to-rent-a-motorbike-in-hanoi/">how to rent a motorbike in Hanoi</a>.</p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#sec-1">How petrol stations work in Hanoi</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-2">Fuel types at Vietnamese pumps</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-3">Fueling a rental bike step by step</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-4">Station etiquette and payment</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-5">Fuel planning for city riding</a></li>
